# The `profile` producer: the image profile marker, as two alternative packages.
#
# Plain `KEY=value` lines only: no logic, no command substitution, no
# expansion. Safe to source from bash and to parse with grep/sed from anything
# else, and checked for that shape by os/rootfs/packages-src/build-deb.sh
# before it is sourced. os/rootfs/packages-src/README.md documents every field.

# Two packages, one payload shape. Exactly one of them is installed into an
# image; they Conflict by name and both Provide `mos-profile`.
PACKAGES="mos-profile-dev mos-profile-prod"

# `all` and not `amd64 arm64`. The entire payload is a 17-byte text file and a
# copyright, with no ELF anywhere, so one archive is correct for every image
# this repository builds and building two would be two names for one thing.
ARCHES="all"
